3. A computer with 3D modeling software (optional)

Let's choose an interesting object to print...

I'll provide you with a simple 3D model file that can be printed using FDM/Fused Deposition Modeling technology. The object is a cute "Robot Bunny" designed by David Thompson, and the STL file is available on Thingiverse.

**Robot Bunny (STL) File:**

You can download the STL file from [Thingiverse](https://www.thingiverse.com/thing:2454418) or copy the following code to create the model:

```
; Robot Bunny
; Author: David Thompson

// Body
sphere(r=10);

// Head
translate([0, 0, 5]) sphere(r=3);

// Eyes
translate([2.5, -1.25, 7.5]) sphere(r=0.75);
translate([-2.5, -1.25, 7.5]) sphere(r=0.75);

// Ears
translate([-4.5, -2, 6]) cube(size=[3, 0.5, 1]);
translate([4.5, -2, 6]) cube(size=[3, 0.5, 1]);

// Legs
translate([-4.5, -7, 5]) cube(size=[3, 1, 1]);
translate([4.5, -7, 5]) cube(size=[3, 1, 1]);
translate([-2.5, -8.5, 5]) cube(size=[5, 0.5, 1]);
translate([2.5, -8.5, 5]) cube(size=[5, 0.5, 1]);

// Arms
